{
  "scope": "Optic and iron-sight render FOV, aim zoom and in-game optic names for all 64 weapon blueprints, from the RPK-74M report that optics look held further out. Field meanings are inferred from values; the BF6 field-name hash algorithm was not identified.",
  "recordedDate": "2026-09-16",
  "build": {
    "label": "1.4.3.0",
    "exactBuildVerified": false,
    "basis": "1.4.3.0 xml-overlay files where present, otherwise the retained 1.4.2.5 XML export. Strings from the 1.4.3.0 fs_us_loc export."
  },
  "inGameConfirmation": [
    "Operator screenshots, 16 SEP 2026: R-MR 1.00x, ROX 1.50x and Mini Flex 1.00x look smaller and further away on the RPK-74M than on the RPKM and M433, and the left arm looks thin and stretched (wider render FOV).",
    "Operator screenshot, 16 SEP 2026: Osa-7 1.00x looks the same on all three weapons (same part, render FOV 38).",
    "Operator confirmation, 16 SEP 2026: iron sights zoom more than 1.00x optics.",
    "Operator screenshots, 16 SEP 2026: SL9, KTS100 MK8 and PW7A2 iron sights from the same position. The range and targets are identical (same 1.50x world zoom); only the weapon size changes, and the KTS100 MK8 (render FOV 18) is drawn much larger. The SL9 (55) looks normal."
  ],
  "fieldMeanings": {
    "Field_7768ebf2": "Weapon (1P) render FOV in degrees. Optic parts hold it on Class_3a930efc; weapon blueprints on Class_76a3b0eb. 55 is the default. The 59 object also links DefaultHipFireRenderFovScale (hip fire).",
    "Class_86ce0d70.Field_65ad1346": "Zoom level camera FOV in degrees: 2*atan(tan(27.5 deg)*pipCameraFactor/zoom); 55 at 1.00x.",
    "Class_86ce0d70.Field_3edbd391": "1/zoom.",
    "Class_86ce0d70.Field_28ae4fd6": "PiP main-camera factor: 1.0 at 1x, rising to 1.5 at 10x. The main camera zooms less than the scope picture.",
    "Class_542ac52c.Field_4f917af5": "Weapon default aiming controller. Every weapon links Aim_1x50 (DefaultBase + 1_5xZoom).",
    "Class_fe7cd16a.Field_4f917af5": "Aim override inside a part. Optic parts use it (for example Aim_01x00_PiP); iron-sight parts do not.",
    "Class_897c99a7.Field_819acc98": "Selector (unlock asset) GUIDs of a weapon part, stored as bare GUID strings.",
    "Class_ccf7da47": "AAM UI record. Field_55aded8d is the internal label. Field_fd698f51 points to Class_fbe1d3bc, whose Field_3d34898a is the in-game name string id. Field_85b318a1 links the AD asset, whose Field_3d34898a ids are the label and description.",
    "Field_149939ab / Field_e9129d03": "Unknown multiplier pair (1.25 or 1.3 in one sub-block of some _Riser/_LowRiser parts). Not the cause: Trijicon MRO parts do not have it, and the MRO looks correct."
  },
  "joinMethod": [
    "Attachment_* Field_157a7d74 gives the U_PRG progression. The ability branch with that progression (Field_f86e0433) lists actions (Class_4ed159fb); their Field_7e54e22c members are the selector GUIDs. These are already resolved as 'selectors' in frosty-optic-category-mapping-2026-09-15.json.",
    "Weapon blueprint Field_0cd9f20f lists parts: external WPM files ('[Ebx] route [guid]', the guid is the Class_897c99a7 object) or inline Class_897c99a7 objects. The part whose Field_819acc98 lists the selector GUID is the part that the attachment enables.",
    "From the part, follow local '[Class_x] guid' pointers (depth 5 is enough) to the object with Field_7768ebf2 and to any Class_fe7cd16a aim override. Without an override, the weapon default aim applies.",
    "Aim controller -> _ZoomLevels references; zoom = 1/Field_3edbd391.",
    "Some attachments also enable an inline U_ATT_* model part with the same selector and no aim. Ignore it when reading aim; it caused about 35 false aim mismatches."
  ],
  "rejectedHypotheses": [
    "Riser model height: the base and _Riser parts of RMR and EFLX use the same visual entity and aim controller.",
    "Field_149939ab/Field_e9129d03 multiplier pair: see fieldMeanings.",
    "Camera or zoom level: both part versions use the same aim controller and zoom level."
  ],
  "findings": {
    "opticRenderFov": {
      "result": "Only RPK74M and L115A3, and the pistols FiveSeven, G22, M18 and M45A1, link the base WPM_SCP_{RMR,RomeoX,EotechEFLX,AcroP2,TrijiconSRO,ShieldCQS} parts, which keep render FOV 55. All other weapons with these optics use _Riser or _LowRiser parts at 40 (ShieldCQS 44). No other optic has a different render FOV between weapons.",
      "affectedWeapons": [
        {
          "weapon": "RPK-74M",
          "internalId": "RPK74M",
          "status": "Confirmed in game for R-MR, ROX and Mini Flex."
        },
        {
          "weapon": "L115",
          "internalId": "L115A3",
          "status": "Source only. Not checked in game."
        }
      ],
