      "notAffected": "Trijicon MRO (RO-M 1.75x): RPK74M links WPM_SCP_MRO and other weapons WPM_SCP_MRO_Tall; both are 34.",
      "uiHint": "The RPK74M and L115A3 AAM records already link riser or mounted AD descriptors (for example AD_RMR_Mounted), so the blueprint links look unintended.",
      "unclear": "M2010ESR: an inline U_ATT_TrijiconSDO part holds 55 beside WPM_SCP_TrijiconSDO (34, Aim_03x50_PiP). Which value applies is not known.",
      "fix": "Link the _Riser versions of the six optics in RPK74M_WB, and probably in L115A3_WB, as RPKM_WB does."
    },
    "ironSights": {
      "result": "No iron-sight part overrides the aim, so every weapon uses Aim_1x50 -> 1_5xZoom (1.50x). 1.00x optics (Aim_01x00_PiP) zoom less than iron sights. The iron render FOV is weapon specific (18 to 50), except SL9 (APDW) and the pistols P18, ES 5.7, GGH-22 and M357 Trait, which keep 55.",
      "siteChange": "data/attachments.json SIGHTS iron name is now 'Iron Sights (1.50x)'.",
      "sl9": "SL9 (APDW) iron sights keep the default 55, the only non-pistol case. Checked in game on 16 SEP 2026: no visible effect (see inGameConfirmation)."
    },
    "labelsVsZoom": "All 1,810 optic part links with their own aim zoom to the magnification in their UI label."
  },
